  "task": {
    "objective": "Two teams contest four physical objectives and transport them to their own homes. Team rewards oppose each other for deliveries and actual captures; teammates share their team payoff.",
    "natural_termination": "All four objectives have been banked, possibly by either team. Otherwise time ends at 96 transitions. Recovery from capture is temporary, not an individual episode end.",
    "interaction": "Bodies block contested passages; a guard tags adjacent opponents and forces them to drop cargo. A hostile mobile decoy within distance two consumes the guard action and is destroyed, allowing an otherwise capturable opponent to escape. Decoys also reduce nearby opposing sight radius from three to one unless a scout pulse restores five. Physical cargo handoffs, local patrol information, public scores and private decoy telemetry create team coordination choices.",
    "observation_access": "Terrain, home locations, score totals and clock are public. Patrol/objective/decoy state is visible within Manhattan radius three, or one when a hostile active decoy is within distance two; a scout pulse raises it to five. Self is always visible. The owner additionally sees its active decoy remotely. Friendly scout signals broadcast only sender position/team globally; hostile signals are visible within distance five. A signal does not reveal the sender inventory or other hidden attributes. Every invisible record has an explicit visibility bit and zero data fields."
  },
